/*!
\page qt-add-qml-preview.html
\ingroup cmake-commands-qtqml

\title qt_add_qml_preview
\keyword qt_add_qml_preview()

\summary{Sets up qmlpreview support for an executable that isn't itself a QML module.}

\cmakecommandsince 6.12
\preliminarycmakecommand

\include cmake-find-package-qml.qdocinc

\section1 Synopsis

\badcode
qt_add_qml_preview(target)
\endcode

\versionlessCMakeCommandsNote qt6_add_qml_preview()

\section1 Description

\c{qt_add_qml_preview()} sets up \l qmlpreview live-reload support for an
executable \c target that loads QML from one or more QML modules created with
\l qt_add_qml_module(), but which is not itself created by
\l qt_add_qml_module(). It creates an additional build target named
\c{<target>_qmlpreview} that launches \l qmlpreview on the executable.

The \c target must be an executable target built by the current project.
Passing a library target, or a target imported from another package, results
in a configure-time error.

If \c target is itself a QML module, this command returns immediately without
doing anything, because such targets already get \l qmlpreview support as part
of \l qt_add_qml_module().

If \c target links against \c{Qt6::Qml} but no in-project QML modules can be
found in its link closure, a warning is emitted at build time, because live
reload of QML embedded in Qt resources will not work in that case. If this
happens, link the \l qt_add_qml_module() target(s) whose QML files you want to
preview to \c target.

\note To make use of the resulting \c{<target>_qmlpreview} target, \c target
      itself needs to be built with
      \l{QML debugging support enabled}{QML debugging infrastructure}, the
      same requirement as for using the \l qmlpreview tool directly.
      Moreover, the target is not created when cross-compiling.

By default, \l qmlpreview support is already set up automatically for every
executable target that links against \c{Qt6::Qml}, so you normally don't need
to call \c{qt_add_qml_preview()} at all. It is only useful as a per-target
override when that automatic behavior has been switched off: calling it enables
\l qmlpreview support for \c target even if preview has been disabled globally
via the \l QT_QML_NO_QML_PREVIEW variable, or for that target via its
\l{cmake-target-property-QT_QML_NO_QML_PREVIEW}{QT_QML_NO_QML_PREVIEW}
property.

\section1 Example

\badcode
qt_add_library(mylib STATIC)
qt_add_qml_module(mylib
    URI My.Lib
    VERSION 1.0
    QML_FILES
        Main.qml
)

qt_add_executable(myapp main.cpp)
target_link_libraries(myapp PRIVATE mylib)

qt_add_qml_preview(myapp)
\endcode

\sa qmlpreview, qt_add_qml_module
*/
